{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>It shall be boiled in it.</b> Also בשלה and מורק and שוטף are of a binyan not called by a verbal noun form, and מורק comes with cholam because of the resh, so that it is not stressed with a dagesh except in a few places, in the pattern לא זורק, after the model of מרקו הרמחים, for the mem is a root letter."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "Reading 'שלא נקרא שם פועלו' literally; the phrase is elliptical and the precise grammatical point Ibn Ezra is making about noun forms is compressed."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:08:50.729446707Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}